On Saturday 19 June 2010 14:58:58 Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> camxes doesn't like "noralujv", but vlatai does.  Just wanted to
> mention that so Pierre and xorxes could make sure that that
> difference represents intention and not accident.

This is known. Camxes does not accept words ending in two consonants. I think 
they are valid (as long as the consonants are a valid medial pair and 
everything else is OK) and cite the example of "ralj" from the Book. I 
ran "noraluj" and "noraluv" through camxes and it took them both.

